{"skill":{"slug":"technical-seo-checker","displayName":"Technical Seo Checker"},"version":{"version":"19.0.0","createdAt":1784906230358,"changelog":"Version 19.0.0 introduces a major cleanup and refactor.\n\n- Removed multiple reference and template files to streamline the skill.\n- Added distribution-manifest.json.\n- Updated SKILL.md metadata to version 19.0.0.\n- No functional logic or audit workflow changes noted.","changelogSource":"auto","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":12320,"sha256":"b12d0a7616ea3eff63b5c11ec17974596e2f99cefbdcaecdf8c991f0fc0be0cb","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"distribution-manifest.json","size":2534,"sha256":"307998a6d6deae34e688870ba22533162d5596cf752040fac49ef3923ab48f1c","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"references/bulk-audit-playbook.md","size":4280,"sha256":"94e1080daf4bb3110a9d8753fe5f3b3dd9117b88dc1123d50c44cd3156b948f5","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/ecommerce-platform-patterns.md","size":3826,"sha256":"e544bd27385af746032f4d4c566326633844e4a20000908eb10a3befcf6265d8","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/http-status-codes.md","size":2529,"sha256":"04c2e9d0b4feba325e48d581cceb7e46093732f9d4c1ce2f8a329ef8b18b1bfb","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/llm-crawler-handling.md","size":4580,"sha256":"d831179bfab06d8a1d73cff9e9fc39a28dab1eab8cf3c69e2bcd4fe8be1dd68f","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/pre-migration-playbook.md","size":6092,"sha256":"b41a708de38ddf822bf37c24d7f8e60f9788b27715dc69725b75dcf756be1202","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/robots-txt-reference.md","size":3138,"sha256":"cb2eba170826f244c6cf653017b4f69379dbd7486aef37a493b975a409d0695d","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/technical-audit-example.md","size":4221,"sha256":"f92ca242d80b70c0e4e6c3cfac497964cf40e304fbacd1253f622646ebdb8680","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/technical-audit-templates.md","size":6368,"sha256":"0db1ed35641046727255d1b22bed57dd7b4feb6e755c9d405b2d494541e37215","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":3338,"sha256":"11354bc7698a2e70ddf8bf122b8e4d0fbee5452647fb987707ff72c502e681b8","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789053527063,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"636af1a91da035a01731ab3823dd450d6710253a0058df4057241ba2611ea38d","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/636af1a91da035a01731ab3823dd450d6710253a0058df4057241ba2611ea38d","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":null,"normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":null,"source":"engines","checkedAt":1784911006845},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":36,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":4,"checkedAt":1789053527063},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This SEO audit skill is mostly coherent, but needs Review because it can send private URLs/page contents to third-party services and persist sensitive SEO metrics without consistent consent controls.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Third-party rendering and validators are useful for SEO audits, but sending rendered DOM, links, URLs, staging hostnames, or query-bearing URLs off-platform is under-scoped for confidential targets. The documented --own-site path also bypasses robots preflight for owned staging hosts without a separate privacy gate.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The package is markdown-only, has a lite capability ceiling, includes no executable scripts, and the manifest lists ordinary 0644 files with inline delivery and canonical-state-read capabilities.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The skill discloses external services such as Firecrawl, crt.sh, W3C validation, IndexNow, and Baidu push, but it does not consistently require informed user consent before third-party rendering of non-public/staging pages or before every persistent save in migration workflows.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The main skill says to ask before saving results, but the pre-migration playbook directly instructs saving rankings, traffic, backlink, redirect maps, and post-migration snapshots to predictable memory paths, which may contain commercially sensitive data and lacks retention, redaction, or access-control guidance.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is technical SEO auditing, and most behavior fits that purpose, including crawls, PageSpeed checks, robots.txt, sitemaps, canonicals, redirects, and migration checks. The index-push helper is purpose-adjacent remediation, not hidden, but it expands the checker from analysis into external write-capable actions.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Install only if users understand that audits may contact third-party SEO/rendering/validation services and may save business-sensitive SEO data locally. For private, staging, authenticated, or tokenized URLs, require explicit approval before external rendering or validation, prefer local tools, strip sensitive query parameters, and confirm any live index-push submissions URL-by-URL.","findings":"[SQP-1] expected: The broad trigger wording can over-invoke the skill for adjacent SEO troubleshooting, but the artifacts still describe a technical SEO checker and this is a scoping quality issue rather than a security defect by itself.\n[SQP-2] expected: Use of external rendering and validation services is normal for technical SEO evidence gathering, but the artifact-backed concern is accepted because private or staging URLs and rendered page content may be transmitted without an explicit consent step.\n[SDI-1] expected: Index submission after fixes is a plausible SEO remediation function and is disclosed as a write channel with dry-run default and --live for submission, so it is not malicious, but live use should require exact user confirmation.\n[SDI-2] expected: The index-push capability goes beyond a pure checker, but the artifact labels it as gated remediation after fixes rather than automatic audit behavior; this remains a Review consideration, not evidence of deception.\n[T09] expected: The Firecrawl fallback is purpose-aligned but materially under-scoped for confidential or staging pages because it can disclose URLs, links, and rendered DOM to a third-party renderer.\n[T09] expected: The migration playbook's memory and CSV saves are purpose-aligned for audit continuity, but they can persist sensitive rankings, traffic, backlink, and migration data in predictable plaintext paths without consistent consent and retention controls.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789053527063}}}}}